tainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1122648-urhanu-\u2013-wtf-wolf-based-werewolves?p=1124361#post1124361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and generally-declining wolf populations. I do like the idea that they were more numerous before humans started hunting down wolves in large numbers</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a lot of Urhanu in Iran, Kazakhstan, Mongolia, Belarus, Ukraine and Russia, which have huge wolf populations (of these nations, wolves are only hunted for bounties in Kazakhstan and Belarus, but given that one of Belarus's most beloved historical kings, who was also king of Russia and Ukraine, was supposed to have been a werewolf....)<br /> <br /> source: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gray_wolf_populations_by_country#Asia\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_o...y_country#Asia</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-03-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:15:55-07:00","id":1124394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1122648-urhanu-\u2013-wtf-wolf-based-werewolves?p=1124388#post1124388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, there is a facet that lets you communicate with animals...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But how intelligent does the fluff describe them as sounding? Just because you can communicate doesn't mean they are on adult human level. Granted, some of them might be, but who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:26:46-07:00","id":1124402,"title":"","content":"Do they need to be? If birds can wrap their heads around consent, I think a wolf could. Animals are not children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:28:43-07:00","id":1124405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1122648-urhanu-\u2013-wtf-wolf-based-werewolves?p=1124394#post1124394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how intelligent does the fluff describe them as sounding? Just because you can communicate doesn't mean they are on adult human level. Granted, some of them might be, but who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not want to break any ones noble images, but animals genera\u0142y thinks 'eat, play, sex or other-things-needed-by-specie'. Cats have <i>literal</i> times when they CRY they want sex ( I'm two female cats owner, I know ). I think if you are werewolf and ask real she-wolf in 'wolf speak' like 'Do you like to mate with me?' and she answer 'Sure!' - you REALLY are as near concent from animal you gonna get. Animals are not sentient ( at least for now ) and they do not have reported deep thoughts - they have instincts, needs and 'fondness' for some beings/people. ( We should generally treat animal as 'smaller people', but they really want to mate / have sex with good looking animal partners. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-03-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:47:49-07:00","id":1124414,"title":"","content":"I think mandatory gaining of either Embarrassing Secret or Notorious Conditions, with violation of the Oath of the Moon as the icing on that cake would be discouraging. Making it not viable for reproduction seems neither more nor less than real life, as in real life its always not viable for reproduction, and wanting a child that will likely be raised with either periods of starvation, dangerous fights, exposure to diseases, and other factors that cause reaching maturity to rates similar to unpleasant third-world countries, or alternatively being raised into what amounts to captivity is more harsh than even hard line Predator Kings or Ivory Claws would care for (though kennel breeding programs offer a tempting level of inconspicuous control over lineages, with a bonus of rapid generation rate might tempt the later).<br /> <br /> It is important to understand both humans and wolves are opportunistic and pragmatic animals, thus Uratha are especially so, so if there is an opportunity that could be exploited likely some Uratha somewhere would be considering or actually doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-03-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:48:34-07:00","id":1124532,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> I resent your notion that somehow having a family in the &quot;third world&quot; is unethical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:23:48-07:00","id":1124791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1122648-urhanu-\u2013-wtf-wolf-based-werewolves?p=1124532#post1124532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> I resent your notion that somehow having a family in the &quot;third world&quot; is unethical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hello Malus,<br /> <br /> First that isn't a notion I have, so any feelings of resentment you may hold are misplaced. Second, &quot;harsh&quot; does not equate to &quot;unethical&quot;. Third is political and off topic because of your use of quotes on third world, so it's in these spoilers/quotes:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Third World is a common vernacular for developing nations to differentiate them from Western Capitalist nations and the Communist Bloc coined by <span style=\"color:#545454\">Alfred Sauvy in the 1950's does not require quotations unless you think it is a </span>pejorative, which in my opinion it is not because I understand the historical context of the phrase (two massive coalitions of <a href=\"http://unqualified-reservations.blogspot.com/2009/01/gentle-introduction-to-unqualified.html\" target=\"_blank\">powers and principalities</a> against each other with everyone else in the middle, so to speak) . </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> As to not distract from a conversation about fictional supernatural part-animal-part-spirit-part-human parents allowing their offspring to starve, get sick and fight as literal wild animals.<br /> <br /> Humans tend to want more safety and security for their offspring than they had, which is a driving force for why civilizations have risen, knowledge and technology progresses. Basically people with hope for greater opportunities and pursuing them to its logical conclusion, slowly accumulating to our present day, with occasional localized dark ages indicating breaks in the systems.<br /> <br /> This is not a matter of ethics, it is driven by a reaction of instinctual reactions caused by natural common mammalian emotional attachments to offspring with the ability to reason. It is neither moral nor immoral, ethical nor unethical but rather an observable fact. I am saying it would be emotionally hard to go through high child mortality rate, especially as a deliberate choice when the option to raise children in civilization which is much safer and comfortable even at the most impoverished end of the spectrum than being a wild animal is available. It may in fact be more ethical to opt out of a comfortable life of consumption and consumerism, but that does not often happen among real life beings able to reason so I think it would be equally emotionally difficult for fictional beings with the ability to reason and mammalian comfort-seeking/nurturing instincts.<br /> <br /> Again harsh does not equate to unethical, and the presumption it does seems odd to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-04-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}